+Recipe 0 has one accepted architecture correction queued before its schema freeze: completed turns that explicitly require further user input may set a host-owned one-next-turn `AWAITING_USER_INPUT` continuation cue. The cue carries no semantic summary; it binds only the immediately preceding completed exchange. Recipe 0 must be able to prefetch that exchange for validation even when the new prompt looks self-contained, and must also be able to discard the prefetch when the new turn is unrelated. This closes the journal-elicitation continuity hole without general history injection. Implementation/tests remain open; evidence: `evidence/phase_a1/A1_R0_OPEN_CONTINUATION_FIX_2026-09-03.md`.
+
